<title>USA: Rite Aid February same-store sales rise.</title>
<headline>Rite Aid February same-store sales rise.</headline>
<dateline>CAMP HILL, Pa. 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Percent change</p>
<p>			   1997     1996    Total   Same-store</p>
<p> Month		 $1,027   $  544    +85.4	+9.0</p>
<p> Quarter		2,657    1,432    +85.7     +10.00</p>
<p> Year		   6,970    5,446    +28.0	+7.9</p>
<p>NOTES: Figures in millions except percentage.</p>
<p>Month is five weeks ended March 1, 1997.</p>
<p>Quarter is 13 weeks ended March 1, 1997</p>
<p>Fiscal Year end is March 1, 1997.</p>
<p>Excluded from February sales is about $31 million in volume from 190 stores in North and South Carolina being sold to J.C. Penney Co. Sixty-three of the units have been transferred to Eckerd Corp, a J.C. Penney unit, in February. The remaining stores have been reclassified as assets held for sale pending the sale to another party by J.C. Penney.</p>
</text>
